# octet npm launcher

`@skaft/octet` is a small, shell-only launcher for the native octet
runtime. npm selects one exact-version platform package through
`optionalDependencies`; the normal `octet` and `octet-host` paths immediately `exec`
the selected native binary.

These scoped names are source packaging identities, not proof of registry rights
or availability. Use the installation command only after an authorized release
has published the packages.

The launcher does not run Node, access the network, download an archive, or
execute an install lifecycle hook. Install it with scripts, audit, and funding
requests disabled:

```sh
npm install --global --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund @skaft/octet@VERSION
```

GNU/Linux uses the glibc x64 package. macOS uses the arm64 or x64 package that
matches the running executable. `octet doctor` reports a missing `rg`
prerequisite.
